@ifnottex
@node Top
@top emacs-devtools-mcp

This manual describes @code{emacs-devtools-mcp}, a Model Context Protocol
server that runs inside Emacs and lets a coding agent inspect frames,
keymaps, faces, buffers, and init.el.

This is a pre-alpha skeleton; sections will be filled in as tool stories
land.

@menu
* Introduction::
* Index::
@end menu
@end ifnottex

@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction

@code{emacs-devtools-mcp} aims to do for Emacs what
@uref{https://github.com/ChromeDevTools/chrome-devtools-mcp,
chrome-devtools-mcp} does for Chrome: give an LLM-driven coding agent a
structured set of tools for inspecting state, exercising input, and
verifying that changes actually rendered.

